     These convenience functions are used to retrieve and update class-depen‐
     dent _E_l_f_3_2___S_y_m_i_n_f_o and _E_l_f_6_4___S_y_m_i_n_f_o records in an ELF object.

     Argument _d_a_t_a is an _E_l_f___D_a_t_a descriptor associated with a section of type
     SHT_SUNW_syminfo.  Argument _n_d_x is the index of the record being re‐
     trieved or updated.  The class-independent _G_E_l_f___S_y_m_i_n_f_o structure is de‐
     scribed in gelf(3).

     Function ggeellff__ggeettssyymmiinnffoo() retrieves class-dependent record at index _n_d_x
     in data buffer _d_a_t_a and copies it to the destination pointed to by argu‐
     ment _s_y_m_i_n_f_o after translation to class-independent form.

     Function ggeellff__uuppddaattee__ssyymmiinnffoo() converts the class-independent record
     pointed to by argument _s_y_m_i_n_f_o to class-dependent form, and writes it to
     the record at index _n_d_x in the data buffer described by argument _d_a_t_a.

